The Gen 1 deployment works but fouls more than expected under variable field chemistry. The result is not treated as failure or hidden as maintenance noise. It directly drives Gen 2 toward better continuous characterization, maintainability and operating-range awareness.

By the closeout date it has:

- the completed Wallaby failure history;
- the Stream 17 commercial reference case with Kelly Gang Mining;
- one operating U.S. Gen 1 reference deployment at Demotte;
- Bedford as its U.S. development and upgrading center;
- additional candidate streams and deployments under disciplined evaluation;
- a high kill rate by design rather than a requirement to convert every target into a project.

Kenji Arakawa remains Cradle leader. Tessa Quinn, Luis Ortega and Maeve Donnelly retain the founding roles already established in canon. This closeout does not manufacture a large department chart or new named executives merely to make the business look mature.
